jobs.description:
As an E&I Maintenance Technician, you will be responsible for maintaining, installing, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial plants. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, and electrical installations to keep industrial processes running smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting instrumentation and electrical systems;
- Testing, calibrating, and commissioning measuring instruments;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance activities;
- Troubleshooting faults in electrical and control systems;
- Ensuring all work complies with safety standards and regulations, including ATEX guidelines.
- You will work independently as well as together with colleagues on industrial projects and maintenance operations.

- MBO level 3 or 4 in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, Mechatronics, or similar;
- Experience with E&I systems in industrial environments;
- Knowledge of NEN 3140 and preferably ATEX;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Accurate, proactive, and solution-oriented mindset;
- Good communication skills in Dutch or English.

As a Shipboard Electrician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical systems onboard ships and maritime installations. You will work with a variety of systems, including power distribution, lighting, navigation equipment, automation systems, and communication networks.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting electrical systems onboard vessels;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Inspecting, testing, and commissioning maritime electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing maintenance and repair activities on onboard systems;
- Supporting refit, modernization, and new-build projects.

You will primarily work at shipyards, ports, and onboard vessels, with occasional travel required for project support and sea trials.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field;
- Relevant experience as an electrician, preferably within shipbuilding, maritime, or offshore environments;
- Knowledge of maritime electrical systems and regulations is an advantage;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Flexible, proactive, and solution-oriented attitude;
- Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English.

Staying active at your own pace, having a chat with the neighbors, and enjoying the fresh air—all while earning a nice extra income of €16.19 per hour (incl. holiday pay)?!💸 As a flyer delivery driver at Spotta in Amsterdam, you set your own flexible schedule, and the team at Tempo-Team is always ready to guide you step-by-step. Sounds like the perfect way to spend your week, right? Read on to see how easy it is!👇

What we offer
- A reliable wage of €16.19 per hour!
- Tempo-Team and Spotta are here to support you!
- No commute—you start right from your front door!
- Healthy work in the fresh outdoors!
- Gear: a sturdy pannier bag and a clear route list!
- A flexible mini-job of 2 to 4 hours per week!

Who you are
You don't need any complex work experience for this role. Because we want to make sure everything runs smoothly for you, the most important thing is that you keep your agreements.

- Available to work 2 to 4 hours per week;
- Available on Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, or Monday (you choose the time!);
- Resident of postal code area 1060 until 1069 in Amsterdam;
- Own a bicycle with a rear luggage rack (for the convenient pannier bags);
- Speak Dutch or English;
- Physically able to lift flyer bundles and walk or cycle to deliver them;
- Comfortable having the flyers conveniently delivered straight to your home.

What will you do
As a flyer delivery driver, you deliver advertising brochures weekly in a fixed, familiar neighborhood near you. On Thursday, Friday, or Saturday, the packages are delivered neatly to your home; you don't even have to stay home for this! After that, you have until Monday evening 19:00 to complete your route. You can arrange your time entirely as you prefer, for example when the sun is shining nicely.

To make things as easy as possible, Spotta provides you with a clear walking list. This shows you the most efficient route along the houses. Would you prefer to walk the route in reverse so that you end closer to home? No pro

As an Electrical Panel Technician, you will be responsible for assembling, wiring, and testing electrical control cabinets and operating panels. You will work from electrical schematics and technical drawings to ensure all systems are built according to the required specifications and quality standards.

Your main responsibilities include:

- Reading and interpreting electrical drawings and diagrams;
- Mounting electrical components and hardware;
- Wiring and assembling control cabinets and panels;
- Testing and inspecting completed systems before delivery;
- Supporting installation or commissioning work when needed.
- Most of your activities will take place in the workshop, with occasional on-site assignments at customer locations.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with panel building or electrical assembly work is preferred;
- Ability to read and understand electrical schematics;
- Accurate and independent working attitude;
- Team player with a hands-on mentality;
- Good command of English (Dutch is an advantage).

As an Industrial Service Electrician, you will perform installation, maintenance, and repair work on industrial electrical systems. You will work on projects involving machinery, control cabinets, cable systems, and power installations. Safety and quality are essential in your daily work.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing industrial cabling and electrical components;
- Maintaining and testing electrical systems;
- Analyzing and solving technical faults;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings;
- Supporting project teams during installation activities.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with industrial electrical installations;
- VCA certification is preferred;
- Knowledge of industrial safety standards is an advantage;
- Flexible and hands-on mentality;
- Good command of Dutch or English.

Are you accurate and do you enjoy working with different materials and machines? For our client in Waalwijk, we are looking for a Production Employee for the Preparation Department. Together with a team of four colleagues, you will transform bulk materials into precisely sized components used in the production of custom-made sandwich panels.

What will you do?

You will work with materials such as foam, wood, and composite. Using production lists, you will cut and calibrate these materials to the required dimensions.

- Adjust materials to the correct thickness using various saws and calibration machines;
- Cut materials to size at your own workstation;
- Calibrate material thickness using a thickness planer;
- Label components according to the production list and sort them onto transport carts;
- Keep your work area clean and organized.

Since every sandwich panel is custom-made, you will work with different production lists and dimensions every day.

What do we expect from you?

- You work accurately and enjoy working as part of a team;
- You can read production lists or are willing to learn;
- You speak Dutch or English.

As an Electrotechnician, you will play a key role in ensuring the reliability and safety of electrical systems. You will work on installation projects, perform maintenance activities, and troubleshoot technical issues to keep operations running smoothly.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing electrical systems and equipment;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations to ensure compliance with safety regulations;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Collaborating with colleagues and customers to deliver high-quality solutions.

This is a varied position where no two days are the same, offering plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills.

- MBO Level 3 diploma in Electrical Engineering or a comparable technical qualification;
- Minimum of 2 years of experience as an Electrotechnician;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B is considered an advantage;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong focus on safety, quality, and precision;
- Ability to work independently as well as part of a team.

Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.

In this position, you will be responsible for assembling, connecting, and maintaining industrial electrical systems. You will work with power distribution systems, cable routes, control panels, and industrial machinery. Together with your team, you ensure that installations operate safely and efficiently.

Your tasks include:

- Installing and connecting industrial electrical equipment;
- Reading electrical diagrams and technical documentation;
- Troubleshooting and repairing electrical malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations and carrying out maintenance work;
- Working together with colleagues and supervisors on-site.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering;
- Experience in industrial electrical work;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain it;
- Knowledge of NEN 1010 and NEN 3140 is a plus;
- Independent and accurate working attitude;
- Dutch or English speaking.

As an Electrical & Instrumentation Technician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial environments. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, electrical panels, and automated installations that are essential for reliable production processes.

Your daily activities include:

- Installing, maintaining, and repairing electrical and instrumentation systems;
- Calibrating, testing, and commissioning instrumentation equipment;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing inspections and preventive maintenance activities;
- Ensuring compliance with safety regulations, including ATEX requirements;
- Supporting production and engineering teams with technical expertise.

Depending on the project, you may work at industrial production sites, processing plants, or workshop facilities.

- Completed MBO level 3 or 4 education in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, or a related technical discipline;
- Relevant experience within industrial electrical engineering or E&I environments;
- Knowledge of NEN standards and ATEX regulations is preferred;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driver’s license B;
- Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
- Good command of the Dutch and/or English language
